  ============================================================================
  Dark Roast: Flash Chilled — iTerm2 Color Scheme
  Version: 5.1.0 Companion

  WHAT IS THIS
  ——————
  A complete iTerm2 color scheme (.itermcolors) implementing the Dark Roast
  design system's ANSI-16 palette. Covers all 16 ANSI colors plus every iTerm2
  chrome key (background, foreground, cursor, selection, bold, badge, tab, link).

  INSTALL
  ———-
  Option A (easiest — double-click):
    1. Double-click "Dark Roast Flash Chilled.itermcolors" in Finder
       (or: open "Dark Roast Flash Chilled.itermcolors" from Terminal)
    2. iTerm2 will import it automatically under Preferences →
       Profiles → Colors → Color Presets → "Dark Roast Flash Chilled"
    3. Select it from the Color Presets dropdown in your profile

  Option B (manual import):
    1. iTerm2 → Settings (⌘,) → Profiles → Colors
    2. Click "Color Presets..." dropdown → "Import..."
    3. Select this file
    4. Select "Dark Roast Flash Chilled" from the Color Presets dropdown

  Option C (apply to all profiles):
    Import as above, then go to each profile and select the preset.
    To set as default for new sessions, update the "Default" profile.

  ABOUT THE FORMAT
  ————————
  iTerm2 stores colors as XML plists where each color is a dict with five keys:
    Alpha Component  — float 0.0–1.0  (1.0 = fully opaque)
    Blue Component   — float 0.0–1.0
    Color Space      — string ("sRGB" for standard, "P3" for wide-gamut)
    Green Component  — float 0.0–1.0
    Red Component    — float 0.0–1.0

  All Dark Roast colors are specified in sRGB. No P3 wide-gamut is used; the
  palette is designed for warm espresso tones, not high-saturation display-P3.

  PALETTE PHILOSOPHY
  —————————
  All four Dark Roast terminal themes (Warp, Tabby, Terminal.app, iTerm2)
  share an identical ANSI-16 palette so that ls, git diff, vim syntax,
  tmux, and every other CLI tool produce exactly the same output regardless
  of which emulator you're running in.

  FULL COLOR REFERENCE
  ——————————
  Chrome:
    background    #D4E1E3   void      — warm-dark deepest layer
    foreground    #000000   crema     — primary text (15.68:1 contrast vs void)
    cursor        #006464   teal      — kinetic cursor, matches editor caret
    cursor text   #D4E1E3   void      — text inside cursor block (inverted)
    selection bg  #9EBEC4   espresso  — warm polished surface (v4: was `grain`)
    selection fg  #000000   crema     — text color on selection
    bold          #000000   crema     — bold text color (same hue, higher weight)
    badge         #B6011C   scarlet   — iTerm2 badge/notification
    tab           #C2D5D9   obsidian  — tab bar background color
    link          #006464   teal      — hyperlink color in terminal output

  ANSI Normal (indices 0–7):
    0  black       #C2D5D9   obsidian  — dark floor (not as deep as void)
    1  red         #B6011C   scarlet   — error / critical
    2  green       #1C6402   sage      — warm fern (terminal extension)
    3  yellow      #7E4F01   amber     — warning / accent
    4  blue        #015E8C   slate     — dusty steel blue (terminal extension)
    5  magenta     #5A129D   mauve     — dried lavender (terminal extension)
    6  cyan        #006464   teal      — live data flow / resolved
    7  white       #000C0F   bone      — reduced-contrast light text

  ANSI Bright (indices 8–15):
    8  bright black    #3B5F65   crater-deep — comment gray, tmux inactive (v4: was `crater`)
    9  bright red      #B6011C   scarlet+  — scarlet companion-bright
    10 bright green    #1C6700   sage+     — sage companion-bright
    11 bright yellow   #725400   gold      — success / stable severity
    12 bright blue     #015E8C   slate+    — slate companion-bright
    13 bright magenta  #6605B3   mauve+    — mauve companion-bright
    14 bright cyan     #006464   teal+     — teal brightened (lighter than #006464;
                                             bright should be visibly brighter)
    15 bright white    #000000   crema     — full brightness
  ============================================================================
-->
